# Google Calendar API Configuration
# ====================================
# For LOCAL development ONLY
#
# SETUP:
# 1. Copy this file: cp .env.local.template .env.local
# 2. Get your API key from: https://console.cloud.google.com/
# 3. In Google Cloud Console:
#    - Create a new project (or select existing)
#    - Enable Google Calendar API
#    - Create an API key credential
#    - Restrict key to Calendar API only (recommended)
# 4. Paste the key value below
# 5. Run Jekyll: GOOGLE_API_KEY=$(cat .env.local | grep GOOGLE_API_KEY | cut -d= -f2) bundle exec jekyll serve
#
# SECURITY:
# - DO NOT commit .env.local to git (already in .gitignore)
# - DO NOT share your API key with others
# - DO NOT commit real API keys to version control
#
# GITHUB DEPLOYMENT:
# - API key is stored in GitHub Secrets as GOOGLE_API_KEY
# - GitHub Actions automatically injects it during build
# - Users on GitHub should NOT need to set this manually

GOOGLE_API_KEY=your_api_key_here
